  "success": true,
  "output": "Here's the consolidated performance analysis across the entire codebase:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis\n\n### 1. N+1 Query Patterns (Backend)\n\n**Critical — `realtime-plugin.ts`**\n\nThe realtime plugin is the worst offender. Every mutation handler loops over rows and fires separate queries per row.\n\n**Comment handler** (`src/server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts` ~L92–144): for each comment, calls `db.post.findUnique()`, then `db.comment.findUnique()` per reply, and `db.user.findMany()` inside `mentionedReaders()`. 10 comments = 30+ queries.\n\nFix — batch-load all posts upfront:\n```typescript\nasync Comment(action, rows) {\n  const db = await getDb()\n  const postIds = [...new Set(rows.map(r => str(r.postId)))]\n  const posts = await db.post.findMany({\n    where: { id: { in: postIds } },\n    select: { id: true, authorId: true, groupId: true }\n  })\n  const postMap = new Map(posts.map(p => [p.id, p]))\n  for (const row of rows) {\n    const post = postMap.get(str(row.postId))\n    // ...\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**`conversationMemberIds()` called 4× for the same ID** (~L296, L325, L337, L346): each call runs a separate `findMany`. Add an in-scope cache:\n```typescript\nconst memberCache = new Map<string, string[]>()\nasync function cachedMemberIds(conversationId: string) {\n  if (memberCache.has(conversationId)) return memberCache.get(conversationId)!\n  const members = await db.conversationMember.findMany({ where: { conversationId }, select: { userId: true } })\n  const ids = members.map(m => m.userId)\n  memberCache.set(conversationId, ids)\n  return ids\n}\n```\n\n**`callTitle()` in `calls.ts` ~L43–67**: fetches the event/conversation once per invitee inside the `for` loop. Fetch it once before the loop.\n\n**`notify.ts` ~L22–28**: creates notifications one by one with `db.notification.create`. Replace with `createMany`:\n```typescript\nif (rows.length > 0) await db.notification.createMany({ data: rows })\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Missing Database Indexes\n\nIn `zenstack/schema.zmodel`, these fields are queried constantly but lack indexes:\n\n| Table | Missing index |\n|---|---|\n| `ConversationMember` | `@@index([conversationId])` |\n| `EventAttendee` | `@@index([eventId])` |\n| `GroupMember` | `@@index([groupId, status])` |\n| `CallParticipant` | `@@index([callId])`, `@@index([userId])` |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Unnecessary Re-renders (Frontend)\n\n**Critical — OrgLayout context value** (`src/components/layout/org-layout.tsx` ~L98–104): the `value` object is created inline every render, causing every `useOrg()` consumer to re-render on any parent state change:\n```typescript\n// BAD: new object reference every render\nconst value = { org, me, role, isAdmin: ..., href: (path) => ... }\n\n// FIX:\nconst href = useCallback((path = \"\") => `/${org.slug}${path === \"/\" ? \"\" : path}`, [org.slug])\nconst value = useMemo(() => ({ org, me: session.user, role, isAdmin: role === \"owner\" || role === \"admin\", href }),\n  [org, session.user, role, href])\n```\n\n**PresenceProvider** (`src/hooks/use-presence.tsx` ~L7–28): a single context value means every online status change re-renders every component that calls `useOnlineUsers()`. Split into a Set context (rarely re-renders) and a selector hook:\n```typescript\nfunction useIsOnline(userId: string) {\n  return useContext(OnlineSetContext).has(userId) // subscribes to Set, not the whole object\n}\n```\n\n**Message grouping function** (`src/components/chat/message-list.tsx` ~L166–175): `sameGroup()` is redefined every render and called for every message pair. Extract it outside the component or memoize with `useCallback`.\n\n**`ReactionSummary`** (`src/components/feed/reactions.tsx` ~L227–229): `counts` Map and sorted `top` array are recomputed every render:\n```typescript\nconst top = useMemo(() => {\n  const counts = new Map<ReactionType, number>()\n  for (const r of reactions) counts.set(r.type, (counts.get(r.type) ?? 0) + 1)\n  return [...counts.entries()].sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1])\n}, [reactions])\n```\n\n**Conversation list filtering** (`src/components/chat/conversation-list.tsx` ~L49–66): `rows` and `filtered` arrays recreated every keystroke. Wrap both in `useMemo` with `[data, q]` deps.\n\n**`emitTyping` in composer** (`src/components/chat/composer.tsx` ~L92–98): wrap with `useCallback` so the reference is stable for any memoized child.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Memory Leaks\n\n**Multiple window listeners per conversation** (`src/components/chat/message-list.tsx` ~L263–275): the `useMarkRead` hook adds `focus`, `blur`, and `visibilitychange` listeners each time a thread mounts. Navigating between conversations accumulates these. Extract to a singleton hook mounted once at the app level.\n\n**Pending socket request timers** (`src/lib/realtime.ts` ~L96–100): `setTimeout` for request timeouts isn't cleared on socket close/unmount. Store the timer ID and clear it in the close handler:\n```typescript\nthis.pendingTimers.set(id, timer)\n// in close handler:\nfor (const t of this.pendingTimers.values()) clearTimeout(t)\nthis.pendingTimers.clear()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. TanStack Query Caching Gaps\n\n**Cache fragmentation on user queries**: five different pickers (calendar, chat, mention, group-add, contacts-rail) all use different query key suffixes (`\"people-picker\"`, `\"chat-picker\"`, `\"mention\"`, etc.) for essentially the same `user.findMany` query. Consolidate with a shared `useOrgMembers(query?)` hook using a single canonical key shape like `[\"user\", \"findMany\", org.id, query]`.\n\n**Tenant-unsafe event key** (`src/components/calendar/use-calendar-events.ts` ~L41`): key is `[\"event\", \"findUnique\", id]` without `org.id`. After switching orgs, a user could get a cached event from the previous org. Fix: `[\"event\", \"findUnique\", org.id, id]`.\n\n**Missing `staleTime` on high-traffic queries**: the default `staleTime: 30_000` causes constant refetches for data the realtime socket already keeps fresh. These should be much higher (5–60 min) and rely on socket invalidation:\n- `app-sidebar.tsx` conversation unread counts and group list (~L58–101)\n- `chat-thread.tsx` conversation + members (~L68–72)\n- `group-members.tsx` group members (~L71)\n- `comments-thread.tsx` comments (~L49)\n- `settings/members-settings.tsx` org members (~L88)\n\n**Missing `placeholderData` on post feed** (`src/components/feed/post-feed.tsx` ~L39–47): causes a UI flicker every time realtime invalidates the feed. Add `{ placeholderData: (prev) => prev }` to the `useDbInfinite` call.\n\n**Over-broad realtime invalidation** (`src/hooks/use-realtime-sync.ts` ~L13–45): a new comment on any post invalidates all post queries site-wide. Consider including `postId` in socket event payloads and invalidating only that post's cache key.\n\n---\n\n### Priority Summary\n\n| Priority | Fix | Estimated impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| P0 | Batch-load in Comment/PostReaction/GroupMember handlers in realtime-plugin | -60–70% query load |\n| P0 | `useMemo` on OrgLayout context value | Eliminates app-wide spurious re-renders |\n| P1 | `createMany` in `notify.ts` | -N queries per notification batch |\n| P1 | Cache `conversationMemberIds` within plugin run | -3× per conversation event |\n| P1 | Fix memory leak in `useMarkRead` window listeners | Prevents listener accumulation |\n| P1 | Add missing DB indexes | Faster lookups on FKs |\n| P2 | Unify user picker query keys | Eliminates duplicate fetches |\n| P2 | Fix tenant-unsafe calendar event key | Correctness + cache safety |\n| P2 | Raise `staleTime` on socket-backed queries | Fewer unnecessary refetches |\n| P3 | Split PresenceProvider context | Reduces presence-change re-renders |\n| P3 | `useMemo` on ReactionSummary, conversation filter, message grouping | Fewer per-render computations |\n| P3 | `placeholderData` on post feed | Better UX, no flicker |\n",
